					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-327845#post-1056020</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-327845/scp-534#post-1056020</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Tue, 15 Mar 2011 23:52:53 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>Dr Blank</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>693148</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>Beautiful, but one thing:</p> <p>You say, "Inhaling SCP-534-1 and SCP-534-3 is lethal. Like SCP-534-1, SCP-534-3 appears to have an indefinite lifespan." This is a little confusing, as it could be read to say that, individually, inhaling either -1 or -3 will result in death. I believe what you mean from context is that inhaling the two while clumped will result in death.</p> <p>It's so minor that you don't even have to fix it. I figured out what you meant, so others most likely will as well.</p> <p>Also really happy to see more from Prometheus labs. As it is, I think only 148 mentions them in the main SCP series.</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
